  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a 5 quart pot over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the onion, carrots, and celery. Cook 4 minutes, stirring often, until the onion looks soft and shiny.",
    "Stir in the cumin, garlic powder, and oregano. Cook 30 seconds until fragrant.",
    "Add the diced tomatoes with their juice, the lentils, the water, and the salt.",
    "Bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce to a steady simmer and partly cover.",
    "Simmer 18 to 20 minutes, stirring now and then, until the lentils and carrots are tender.",
    "Stir in the pepper and lemon juice. Taste and add a pinch more salt if needed.",
    "Ladle into bowls. Cool leftovers fully before storing in the fridge or freezer, and add a little water when reheating."
  ],
